title: Passive detection + surfacing of newer c2c release available upstream
updated_at: "2026-07-21T14:11:38Z"
---
Passive detection + surfacing of a newer c2c release available upstream. Today
upstream-release detection is PULL-ONLY via `c2c self-update --check-only` (hits
the GitHub releases API synchronously); nothing tells an operator/agent that a
newer release exists unless they run that command. Post-upgrade changelog
auto-show (B126) and local stale-binary self-restart (I010/C2c_stale) are
already automatic, but neither reports "a newer release is available upstream."

GOAL: a low-cost, non-blocking, offline-safe "newer release available" nudge on
the surfaces below. Never a synchronous network call on a hot path.

VERSION SOURCE (decided): reuse the already-warmed remote changelog cache as the
primary signal — the changelog machinery already background-fetches CHANGELOG.md
(`C2c_changelog.spawn_background_fetch` / `cache_is_stale` from the SessionStart
hook), and each release adds a versioned entry. "Newer version known" =
`merged_entries` filtered by `compare_version e.version Version.version > 0` on
remote-sourced entries. No new synchronous network path. Freshness is bounded by
the existing background-fetch cadence. (GitHub releases API remains the
authoritative asset source used by `self-update`; a cached daily releases-API
check is a possible follow-up if changelog freshness proves insufficient, but is
NOT required for v1.)

ALSO detect newer RELAY versions (decided): the relay reports its version via
`/health` (and `c2c doctor relay` already reads it). Compare the connected
relay's reported version against (a) the client's own version and (b) the latest
known version from the changelog cache, and surface when the relay you're talking
to is behind the latest known release (informational — a client cannot upgrade a
remote relay, but it flags "prod relay is stale, consider deploying"). Fail
closed / silent when the relay is unreachable or reports no version.

SURFACES (all decided in):
1. `c2c doctor` — add a line: newer release X available (you're on Y); run
   `c2c self-update`. Also a relay-version line when the relay is behind latest
   known. Pull-only, zero hot-path cost. SAFEST first slice — do this first.
2. `c2c health` / `server_info` — add `latest_known_version` +
   `update_available:bool` (client) and a relay-version-vs-latest field, from the
   cache only, so tooling/MCP callers can read it programmatically.
3. SessionStart injection — piggyback the changelog auto-show path
   (`c2c_hook_cmd.ml`): inject a one-line "newer release available" once per
   version, rate-limited, marker-guarded exactly like changelog auto-show (never
   regress marker; downgrade/equal = no-op; offline = silent). Keep it to ONE
   line so it doesn't bloat session context.
4. `c2c version` / `c2c --version` — MUST STAY FAST: read the cache ONLY, never
   fetch. If the cache already knows a newer version, append a single trailing
   line ("(newer release X available — run c2c self-update)"); otherwise print
   version exactly as today. A network call here is forbidden — `--version` is
   used in scripts and hot paths (e.g. `c2c_gui_cmd.ml` invokes `c2c --version`).

HARD CONSTRAINTS:
- No synchronous network I/O on `--version`, `version`, SessionStart hook, or any
  other hot path. All reads come from the local changelog cache; the only network
  activity is the EXISTING background fetch.
- Offline / stale-cache / cache-missing = silent no-op everywhere (never an error,
  never a warning that breaks scripts parsing `--version`).
- Respect the existing marker/rate-limit discipline for the SessionStart nudge so
  it shows at most once per version per client.
- Agent-facing text stays terse (one line).

IMPLEMENTATION SKETCH:
- Add a small helper, e.g. `C2c_changelog.latest_known_newer ~current` returning
  `string option` (highest remote-cached version strictly greater than current,
  else None) — pure over the already-loaded cache, no I/O.
- doctor / health / version / hook each call it and format per-surface.
- Relay-behind check: `C2c_doctor_relay` (or health) compares relay `/health`
  version to `latest_known` from the same helper.
- Tests: hermetic — seed a changelog cache with a newer entry, assert each
  surface reports it; assert offline/empty-cache = silent; assert `--version`
  performs no network call (fixture-gate any network, or assert timing/paths).

ACCEPTANCE:
- With a newer version in the changelog cache: doctor, health JSON, SessionStart
  (once/version), and `--version` all surface it.
- Offline or no newer version: every surface is silent/normal; `--version` is
  byte-identical to today except the optional trailing line.
- Relay-behind-latest surfaced in doctor/health when applicable.
- No new synchronous network path; `--version` timing unchanged.